<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Front for the Liberation of Occupied South Yemen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1966">1966</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FLOSY</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Front for the Liberation of Occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> (FLOSY) was a nationalist movement formed in 1966 and backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Nasser</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, which fought the British in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden-emergency">Aden Emergency</a>. It competed violently with the more radical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> for control of the independence struggle. By late 1967 the National Liberation Front had defeated it, and FLOSY's leaders went into exile when South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> became independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/front-for-the-liberation-of-occupied-south-yemen.jpg" alt="Front for the Liberation of Occupied South Yemen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 愛喝奶茶 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Front_for_the_Liberation_of_Occupied_South_Yemen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
